What is a Loop?
Section of code in a program
which is executed repeatedly, 
until a specific condition is satisfied
For Aptech Centre Use Only
Elementary Programming with C/Session 6/ 4 of 21
3 types of Loop Structures
The for loop
The while loop
The do….while loop
For Aptech Centre Use Only
Elementary Programming with C/Session 6/ 5 of 21
The for loop-1
Syntax
 The initialize counter is an assignment statement that sets
the loop control variable, before entering the loop
 The evaluation parameter defines how the loop control 
variable changes, each time the loop is executed
 The conditional test is a relational expression, which 
determines, when the loop will exit
For Aptech Centre Use Only
Elementary Programming with C/Session 6/ 6 of 21
 The three sections of the for loop must be separated by a
semicolon(;)
 The statement, which forms the body of the loop, can 
either be a single statement or a compound statement
 The for loop continues to execute as long as the 
conditional test evaluates to true. When the condition 
becomes false, the program resumes on the statement 
following the for loop
The for loop-2
For Aptech Centre Use Only
Elementary Programming with C/Session 6/ 7 of 21
